Spec: LibTofu

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Low-level OpenTofu command wrapper shared by the tofu install/delete stage: map a package
    option descriptor to an HCL type expression, render any value as an HCL literal through
    `tofu console` itself, and drive one working directory of `.tf` sources through
    init, plan, apply, destroy and outputs — throwing on tofu failure so callers can record
    state instead. The generating layer that feeds these commands is ./tofu_gen.rhai.

Exposes:
  @get_tf_type(item, optional) — HCL type expression for one schema-like descriptor; consumed
    by the gen layer to write `variable` blocks.
  @to_tf(v) — HCL literal text for any serializable @rhai value, produced by piping
    `jsondecode(<escaped>)` into `tofu console`.
  @run_init(path) — seeds `${path}/.tofurc` then `tofu init`.
  @run_plan(path) — `tofu plan` to the `tf.plan` plan file.
  @run_apply(path) — applies the `tf.plan` plan file.
  @run_destroy(path) — destroys the configuration (an `apply -destroy` re-plan, not a
    plan-file reversal).
  @get_output(path) — raw `tofu output -json` stdout text.
  All six are reached as `tf::...` through `import "tofu" as tf` by the gen layer and by the
    per-kind stage scripts (Depends on); nothing else in the crate imports this module.

Accepts:
  @path — @String tofu working directory; every caller passes `${package_dir}/tofu`. Checked
    for nothing and interpolated unquoted into the `sh -c` line.
  @item — descriptor @rhai map: @.type one of `string`, `integer`, `number`, `boolean`,
    `object`, `array`, plus @.properties (object) or @.items (array). JSON-decoded shapes,
    not validated.
  @optional — @bool driving the `optional(...)` wrapper.
  @v — any @rhai value reaching @json_encode_escape (maps, arrays, strings, numbers, bools,
    unit — unit serializes to JSON `null`).

Returns:
  @run_init, @run_plan, @run_apply, @run_destroy return unit on success; @tofu's own stdout,
    stderr and the @shell_run rc are all discarded beyond the zero test.
  @get_output returns the verbatim `tofu output -json` stdout text — a JSON document on
    success; this file decodes and trims nothing (callers @json_decode it themselves).
  @to_tf returns the verbatim `tofu console` stdout — the HCL rendering of the decoded value,
    trailing newline included; no trim happens in the binding or here.
  @get_tf_type returns one expression, e.g. `optional(number)` or
    `object({host = optional(string), port = optional(number)})`.

Raises:
  @throw with a fixed literal when @shell_run yields a non-zero exit: `tofu init failed`,
    `tofu plan failed`, `tofu apply failed`, `tofu destroy failed`. The rc and the tofu text
    are not in the message — they went to the process-inherited stdio only. Every message is
    a bare string, so callers catch an interpreter error, not a typed result.
  Engine-side raise, unhandled here, from the four host functions this file calls:
    `sh` spawn failure; @shell_output non-zero exit (engine text embeds
    `Command failed, rc=N`); @shell_output with exit zero but any stderr content
    (`Command had stderr : ...`) — so a tofu warning or notice written on stderr fails
    @get_output and @to_tf even when tofu succeeded; non-UTF-8 stdout; @file_write failing,
    notably @run_init on a missing `${path}` since the binding never creates parent dirs.
  @get_tf_type raises only on malformed descriptors: an `object` without @.properties dies on
    the chained @.keys() over the missing-key read. A missing or unknown @.type raises
    nothing — the switch has no default arm and the fn returns @rhai::Dynamic unit silently.

Handles:
  Exactly one decision shape in the run lane: exit code equal to zero or not. No `try`
    catch, no retry, no stderr parsing, no partial-success grading; any non-zero rc collapses
    to the same per-fn literal throw.
  Descriptor shape branches in @get_tf_type: `integer` and `number` collapse to one `number`
    answer; an `items` that is JSON `null` or absent answers `list(any)`; an empty
    `.properties` answers `map(any)` — each with the `optional(...)` wrapper when @optional.
  Unit values passed to @to_tf: they serialize as JSON `null` and round-trip through
    `tofu console` as HCL `null`.

Must:
  Invoke the `tofu` binary through PATH inside `sh -c` lines fixed per fn: @to_tf runs
    `echo 'jsondecode(<escaped>)'|tofu console`; @run_plan runs
    `cd ${path};tofu plan -input=false -out=tf.plan -var-file=vynil.tfvars`; @run_apply runs
    `cd ${path};tofu apply -input=false -auto-approve tf.plan`; @run_destroy runs
    `cd ${path};tofu apply -destroy -input=false -auto-approve -var-file=vynil.tfvars`;
    @get_output runs `cd ${path};tofu output -json`. Only @run_init sets any environment —
    the inline `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE=.tofurc` prefix on the @tofu process itself; no
    `TF_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR` or other TF_* value appears anywhere (the engine @get_env is never
    called). The `tofu` name resolves to the opentofu `1.11.6` pinned by the image.
  Write `${path}/.tofurc` before starting @tofu in @run_init, overwriting on every call, with
    a fixed CLI config: a `filesystem_mirror` at `/nonexistent/.terraform.d/plugins`
    including `*/*` plus a `direct {}` fallback — mirror the provider tree the image seeds at
    that path, with network download as fallback; the relative `.tofurc` reference pairs with
    the leading `cd`, and the file is written even when tofu then fails.
  Keep `@run_apply` a pure plan-file execution: it never re-reads `vynil.tfvars` and fails if
    `tf.plan` is absent or stale. Keep @run_destroy independent of `tf.plan`: it re-plans the
    configuration with `-destroy` and needs `vynil.tfvars` present; its throw label says
    destroy while the verb is `tofu apply -destroy`.
  Keep the plan-file and var-file names `tf.plan` and `vynil.tfvars` as the frozen pair with
    the gen layer, whose @gen_tfvars writes `vynil.tfvars` into the same directory every
    stage script passes as @path.
  Let the @to_tf pipeline carry the value through three escape layers: @json_encode_escape
    emits the serde JSON double-quoted one further level, the HCL string literal decodes back
    to exactly that JSON text, @jsondecode parses it, and `tofu console` prints the HCL
    form. The single quotes around the echoed word are a shell-layer fact: nothing here
    escapes an apostrophe inside @v before splicing.
  Freeze the @get_tf_type mapping: `string` to `string`, `integer` to `number`, `number` to
    `number`, `boolean` to `bool`; an `object` recurses every @.properties entry with
    @optional `true` regardless of any `required` list, joining `k = t` with `, `; an `array`
    with a concrete `items` recurses with @optional `false`; @optional wraps the finished
    expression as `optional(...)` for object and array only at the level asked. Property
    order in the `object({...})` text is the @rhai map @ iteration order (BTreeMap-backed).
  Touch no tfstate: no fn here reads, writes or moves any `.tfstate`; the state save and
    restore around installs is the per-kind install_tofu scripts' contract.
  Evaluate nothing at import: the file is seven @fn definitions and zero top-level statements,
    so importing the module performs no I/O and defines no globals.

Depends on:
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — @shell_run, @shell_output (`shell` registrar), @file_write
    (`fs` registrar), @json_encode_escape (json helper); script surface installed by the
    engine assembly behind ./../../../common/src/rhaihandler.sdd, including the fact that a
    mock engine keeps these host powers live.
  `tofu` CLI workflow contracts owned elsewhere: the plan-file exchange between
    `plan -out` and bare `apply`, `apply -destroy`, `output -json`, console stdin evaluation,
    and CLI-config `filesystem_mirror` semantics.
  /agent/Dockerfile + /agent/providers.tf — the pinned @tofu build and the build-time
    `tofu init` whose result the image seeds at `/nonexistent/.terraform.d/plugins`, the tree
    @run_init's mirror line points at.
  ./tofu_gen.rhai — sole @get_tf_type and @to_tf consumer; its spec ./tofu_gen.sdd is being
    authored (pending reference target).
  ../system/install_tofu.rhai, ../service/install_tofu.rhai, ../tenant/install_tofu.rhai,
    ../system/delete_tofu.rhai, ../service/delete_tofu.rhai, ../tenant/delete_tofu.rhai —
    the @run_init/@run_plan/@run_apply/@run_destroy/@get_output callers; installs catch this
    module's throws and record status, which is why the message content may change freely but
    the throw-vs-return polarity may not.

Tasks:
  [?] @to_tf quoting and @path interpolation: the echoed word breaks on the first apostrophe
      inside @v (nothing escapes `'` before splicing into `echo '...'`), and unquoted
      `${path}` splits on spaces — both feed caller package text straight into an `sh -c`
      line. Decide whether to rebuild the commands quote-safely (e.g. printf with separate
      quoted segments) or to record a caller-side charset limit.
  [?] A @tofu killed by a signal is reported by @shell_run as exit `0` and therefore takes the
      success branch; the compound also uses `;` after `cd`, so @tofu runs in the engine's
      working directory even when `${path}` does not exist and only its rc decides. Decide
      whether run_* must detect signal deaths and guard the `cd`.
  [?] @get_tf_type has no catch-all @switch arm: a descriptor with a missing or unknown
      @.type returns @rhai::Dynamic unit with no error, which the gen layer then interpolates
      into generated `.tf` text. Decide whether the mapping edge must throw instead.
  [ ] Map tests into /agent/tests/rhai_tofu_gen.rs — that file imports only `tofu_gen`
      (@has_tofu_files, @gen_provider, @provider_constraint) and drives none of the six fns
      here: add a pure @get_tf_type table case, and a fake-`tofu`-on-PATH case for
      `@run_init` (asserting the written `.tofurc` and the throw text) and @get_output's
      stderr trap.
  [ ] Re-resolve the ./tofu_gen.sdd reference once the gen-layer spec lands.

Done when:
  The five scenarios have passing mapped tests or recorded decisions, the quoting and
    signal-detection decisions are settled, and `specdd lint` is green on this file.

Scenario: run_init writes the mirror config even when tofu fails
  Given `${path}` exists and is writable, and `tofu` on PATH exits non-zero for `init`
  When @run_init(path) runs
  Then `${path}/.tofurc` exists and names `/nonexistent/.terraform.d/plugins` and `direct`
  But the call raises with exactly the text `tofu init failed`

Scenario: plan freezes vylin.tfvars by name
  Given a tofu directory with valid `.tf` sources but no `vynil.tfvars`
  When @run_plan(path) runs
  Then the @tofu exit is non-zero for the unread var-file and the call raises `tofu plan failed`
  And no case exists where @run_plan succeeds without `vynil.tfvars`

Scenario: destroy re-plans instead of reversing the plan file
  Given a directory where @run_plan succeeded and `tf.plan` was then deleted
  When @run_apply(path) runs it raises `tofu apply failed`, unread plan file
  But @run_destroy(path) succeeds when `vynil.tfvars` and the sources are still present
  And @run_destroy never opens `tf.plan`

Scenario: get_output rejects a zero-exit warning
  Given a @tofu double (fake binary) that exits `0`, prints valid JSON on stdout and any
    notice on stderr
  When @get_output(path) runs through @shell_output
  Then the call raises with the engine `Command had stderr` text rather than returning the JSON

Scenario: descriptor table and recursion
  Given the descriptors `#{type: "integer"}`, `#{type: "object", properties: #{host:
    #{type: "string"}}}`, `#{type: "array", items: #{type: "boolean"}}` and
    `#{type: "array", items: null}`
  When @get_tf_type runs on each with @optional `true`
  Then the answers are `optional(number)`, `object({host = optional(string)})`,
    `optional(list(bool))` and `optional(list(any))`
  But @get_tf_type on `#{type: "tuple"}` returns unit and raises nothing
